        <p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest text-indigo-600 uppercase mb-4">Autumn &middot; October &middot; Xi&rsquo;an</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-zinc-900 mb-3">Golden Light and Ancient Stones</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">8:00 AM. You are the first person through the doors at the Terracotta Warriors museum. Pit 1 stretches before you in silence &mdash; 2,000 clay soldiers, each face unique, bathed in the low golden light of an October morning. No jostling, no selfie sticks. Just you and two millennia of history. After lunch at the Muslim Quarter &mdash; hand-pulled biangbiang noodles, cumin-dusted lamb skewers, a pomegranate juice for the road &mdash; you bike the 14-kilometer Xi&rsquo;an City Wall as the sun sets behind the Bell Tower. The air is crisp, 19&deg;C, the perfect temperature for a sweater and a sense of wonder. Dinner is hot pot, and the conversation is about how this might be the best day of the trip.</p>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 text-xs text-indigo-700 font-medium">
          <span>19&deg;C</span><span>&middot;</span><span>6 rain days</span><span>&middot;</span><span>&rarr; After Oct 8: perfect</span>
